0	71	Jutta Pauliina Urpilainen (born 4 August 1975) is a Finnish politician.
72	178	She was the first female chair of the Social Democratic Party of Finland, which she led from 2008 to 2014.
179	277	She was the Minister of Finance as well as the Deputy Prime Minister of Finland from 2011 to 2014.
278	410	Between 2019 and 2024, she served as the European Commissioner for International Partnerships in the first von der Leyen Commission.
411	515	Urpilainen was a candidate in the 2024 election for President of Finland, receiving 4.3% of the vote.



515	642	Early life and education
Born in Lapua, Southern Ostrobothnia, Urpilainen is the daughter of former politician Kari Urpilainen.
643	744	She studied at the University of Jyväskylä, where she graduated with a Master's of Education in 2002.
745	815	During her undergraduate studies, she spent an Erasmus year in Vienna.
816	883	She worked as a school teacher until her election to Parliament.



883	1003	Political career


Early beginnings
Urpilainen served as president of the Young European Federalists of Finland in 2001.
1004	1043	She joined the Kokkola city in 2001.



1043	1183	Member of Parliament and party leadership
Urpilainen was a member of Parliament for the Vaasa constituency from the 2003 national elections.
1184	1303	In parliament, she was a member of the Committee on Education and Culture and a deputy member of the Finance Committee.
1304	1440	In addition to her parliamentary work, she was also a member of the Advisory Council of the Finnish Institute of International Affairs.

1440	1601	Urpilainen was elected as the chair of the Social Democratic Party in June 2008, succeeding former Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Finance Eero Heinäluoma.
1602	1713	She won on the second ballot, defeating former Minister for Foreign Affairs Erkki Tuomioja by 218 votes to 132.
1714	1816	During her tenure from 2008 until 2014, support for the Social Democrats fell from 21 to 15.5 percent.
1817	1906	However, in the 2011 elections, she returned the party to government after four years.



